---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import CTA from '@/components/sections/CTA.astro';

const pageTitle = 'About';
const pageDescription =
  'Learn about ConcordiaSpring — yoga and somatic practice in Asheville, NC. Grounded classes, small groups, and a teacher who meets you where you are.';
---

<PageLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 px-6 border-b border-border/60">
    <div class="container max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold text-foreground">
        About ConcordiaSpring
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        A small school for yoga and somatic practice in Asheville — where the pace is human, the
        room is quiet enough to hear yourself, and showing up counts more than performing well.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 px-6">
    <div class="container max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold text-foreground mb-8">The School</h2>
      <div class="space-y-6 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          ConcordiaSpring grew from a simple conviction: the body already knows how to heal, settle,
          and find its way home. Our work is not to fix you or push you toward someone else&apos;s
          idea of wellness. It is to create conditions where you can feel what is actually here —
          breath, weight, sensation, presence — and practice from that honesty.
        </p>
        <p>
          Classes are small on purpose. Workshops go deeper into somatic inquiry. Nothing is built
          for spectacle or scale. We are not trying to be the biggest studio in town. We are trying
          to be a place where you are recognized when you walk in the door.
        </p>
        <!-- [PLACEHOLDER] Expand with origin story, naming, or community context when ready -->
        <p>
          The name points toward concord — agreement, harmony — and spring as both season and source.
          Practice here is relational: with yourself, with the room, with what moves through the
          body when it is given time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-muted py-16 md:py-20 px-6">
    <div class="container max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,240px)] md:items-start">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold text-foreground mb-8">The Teacher</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              Christopher teaches yoga and somatic practice in Asheville. He is a somatic coach, a
              writer, and a former freediving instructor — work that taught him how much intelligence
              lives below the level of words.
            </p>
            <p>
              He holds a degree in computer science from Berea College. That path may seem unrelated,
              but it sharpened his attention to systems: how parts relate, where friction lives, and
              what happens when you slow down enough to notice the whole.
            </p>
            <!-- [PLACEHOLDER] Personal teaching philosophy, certifications, years of practice -->
            <p>
              In class, he favors clarity over charisma. You will find precise guidance, room for
              your own experience, and an atmosphere that takes your inner life seriously without
              making it precious.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure>
          <!-- TODO: Replace placeholder with teacher photo
          <img
            src="/images/christopher.jpg"
            alt="Christopher, teacher at ConcordiaSpring"
            class="w-full rounded-xl object-cover aspect-[3/4]"
            width="480"
            height="640"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          -->
          <div
            class="aspect-[3/4] w-full max-w-xs mx-auto md:mx-0 rounded-xl border border-border bg-card flex items-center justify-center"
            role="img"
            aria-label="Teacher photo placeholder"
          >
            <span class="text-sm text-muted-foreground px-4 text-center">Photo coming soon</span>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 px-6">
    <div class="container max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold text-foreground mb-8">The Space</h2>
      <div class="space-y-6 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        <!-- [PLACEHOLDER] Studio name, address, parking, accessibility notes -->
        <p>
          Classes are held in Asheville, NC. Exact location and directions are shared when you book
          — we keep the address private until registration so the space stays calm and unhurried for
          those who are already on their way.
        </p>
        <p>
          Bring a mat if you have one. The room is kept simple: enough light, enough quiet, nothing
          that competes with the practice.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA
    title="Come to a class"
    description="See what is currently offered and reserve your spot. No experience required — just willingness to arrive."
    cta={{ href: '/offerings', label: 'View offerings' }}
  />
</PageLayout>
